{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"empirical-inhuman-urus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nMultiple production bugs (3435, 3a33, 4dd2, 4c6c class) came from store write paths that bypassed the locked write seam (run_git_write / ticket_txn) with raw 'git add/commit/rm' — including inside GitHub workflow YAML and scripts. The routing campaign fixed known sites; nothing prevents new bypasses.\n\n## Approach\nDeterministic CI lint scanning src/rebar, scripts, and .github/workflows for raw git write invocations (add/commit/rm/mv/update-ref against the tickets tracker) outside the canonical seam modules. Allowlist file for the legitimate seam internals (gitutil.py, lock.py, migration/bootstrap paths), each entry with a reason comment. Failure message teaches: route through run_git_write or extend the seam. Pattern precedent: module-size gate (single-sourced config, teaching error).\n\n## Scope\n- new lint script (Python) + CI wiring in the verify workflow\n- allowlist file with seam internals\n- remediation of any bypass sites the first full scan finds\n\n## Testing\nLint unit tests: seam-internal file passes via allowlist; raw commit in a workflow YAML fails with the teaching message; allowlist entry without reason fails. Full-tree run is clean at merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] CI fails on any raw git write against the store outside allowlisted seam modules, across Python, shell, and workflow YAML.\n- [ ] Allowlist entries require a reason; the error message names the seam APIs to use.\n- [ ] Tree is clean at landing (all existing bypasses routed or allowlisted with justification).\n- [ ] Lint has its own unit tests.","id":"d37e-4f64-3265-4f30","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":["gates","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Raw-git-write CI lint: enforce the canonical locked store write seam"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785640012640201001,"uuid":"91a4fc56-966e-4d2c-94e9-e5663bac6dd3"}